g'>+0.26\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.17 to +0.34), about +3.1\u00b0F since 1904. Kingman's average high shows no clear change: +0.07\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.04 to +0.18) that includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1980, lows show no clear change and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.91\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.62 to +1.21). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 8 of 12 months. Highs rose in none.","t_rain":"Kingman has gotten drier","p_rain":"Kingman's yearly precipitation has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.35 inches per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.55 to \u22120.15), about \u22124.2 inches since 1904. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 8.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 1919 (21.22 in); the driest, 1947 (3.58 in). Kingman almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 18 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}